# Normalise line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) while CI runs on ubuntu-latest, so
# without this the two disagree about every file. It also fixed a concrete problem: git's
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning was being parsed by lint-staged as the output of
# `git stash create`, which broke the pre-commit hook with "fatal: Needed a single revision"
# until `core.safecrlf=false` was set locally as a workaround.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, storing LF in the repository and checking out
# the platform's native ending. Existing files are NOT renormalised -- that would rewrite
# nearly every file for no functional gain. This governs files from here on.
* text=auto

# Always LF: shell scripts and anything executed inside Linux containers or CI, where CRLF
# is a syntax error rather than a cosmetic difference.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch, never diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
